./" Manpage for mkcp
.TH man 1 "31 August 2025" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
	mkcp - mkdir, cp things there
.SH SYNOPSIS
	mkcp source[s] destination
.SH DESCRIPTION
	makes the destination directory. then copies the files there. if dest already exists it's just cp
.SH OPTIONS
	cp default options work, so -i to prompt before overwrite, -n to not overwrite, -b to make backups, -u for update, -v for verbose. Copies directories by default (-r)
.br
	mkdir default options do not work because mkdir only uses the last argument
.SH EXAMPLES
	mkcp *.csv csvs
.br
	mkcp sdifji.py ../../ijsdif
.SH BUGS
	probably none
